Water quality is related to a use and a place (@wu-purpose: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @water-and-sanitation, #source "../sources/Drinking-Water-Quality-WHO-2026.lingua#r_71BB45J2CZ76C0WZ6H1C7SWZ5F", #source "../sources/Industrial-Water-Treatment-UFC-3-230-13.lingua#r_41KNKBCA6GZWQ6VAJGAPG2HJ3R", #water-and-sanitation "../../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/practice/Mass-and-component-balances.lingua#r_163GVDJGRJ1DD4JT2398GM371H") { r_3WKPW5Q04M3S2KF8EPB2K0FTDK
**Read:** [Guidelines for drinking-water quality — WHO, 2026 consolidated edition](../sources/Drinking-Water-Quality-WHO-2026.lingua#r_71BB45J2CZ76C0WZ6H1C7SWZ5F), the conceptual framework and microbial, chemical and acceptability chapters; [Industrial Water Treatment Operation and Maintenance — UFC 3-230-13](../sources/Industrial-Water-Treatment-UFC-3-230-13.lingua#r_41KNKBCA6GZWQ6VAJGAPG2HJ3R), chapters 2–3, industrial purposes and makeup water.

Drinking water, irrigation water, boiler feed, cooling water and semiconductor rinse water answer different questions. A constituent important to one use may be irrelevant to another, and a treatment that meets one purpose can leave an important hazard or performance problem for another.

Describe a requirement as a constituent or property, its basis and unit, the location and time of assessment, a measurement method and a justified criterion. Include physical delivery conditions such as pressure, temperature and availability. Distinguish an aesthetic observation, a health-based requirement, an ecological condition and an equipment specification.

For one water sample, ask separately about microbial quality, particles, dissolved ions, organic matter and the relevant trace contaminants. Conductivity alone cannot identify all dissolved chemicals; clarity cannot establish absence of pathogens. An industrial grade does not automatically establish potability. Connect each proposed measurement with the decision it can support.

